  "published": "2026-11-23T08:17:49.75Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking changes:\n- Casting a null string to an ISO 639 language struct throws InvalidCastException.\n- Casting a string that isn't an ISO 639 code to an ISO 639 language struct throws InvalidCastException.\n- `Iso15924Extensions.GetDate` and `Iso15924ScriptCodeAttribute.Date` return `DateTime?` on every target, including `net10.0`, where they returned `DateOnly?`. A .NET Standard library that calls them no longer fails with `MissingMethodException` in a `net10.0` app. On .NET 6 and later, use `DateOnly.FromDateTime` to get a `DateOnly`.\n- `IStringEnum` no longer extends `IConvertible` on any target. A struct that implements `IConvertible` declares it itself; the ISO 639 structs still do on `netstandard2.0` and `net10.0`. Code that uses an `IStringEnum` as an `IConvertible` needs a cast.\n\nFixed:\n- CodeAttributeBase.EnglishNames and FrenchNames return a copy, so changing the returned array no longer changes the attribute's names.\n- The package now includes its XML documentation, so IntelliSense shows member descriptions.\n\nDeprecated and removed:\n- `Iso639LanguageType.Ancient` is obsolete. ISO 639:2023 merged the ancient language type into `Historical`, and no ISO 639-3 code has it.\n\nChanged:\n- On .NET Standard, the name parameters of every `Iso639LanguageCodeAttribute` constructor are annotated `[DisallowNull]`.\n- The package's NuGet tags include `ISO 15924` and `script`.",
